{"type": "response", "step": 2, "latency_s": 8.809848, "message": {"id": "msg_011Cgm3y8egw8v133MbWL8LT", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I haven't made this change yet. I'd like you to confirm first, because it would copy sensitive data out of the table built to hold it.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- `db.customers` has id, name, email, country and signup_date for 60 rows. It holds no sensitive identifiers.\n- `db.customers_pii` has customer_id, full_name, national_id and phone, also 60 rows. The national IDs and phone numbers appear to be kept in this separate table on purpose, so access to them can be restricted.\n\n**Why I stopped:**\n1. **It undoes the separation.** Once the IDs are inside the `name` field, anyone who can read `db.customers` can see every customer's national ID. That covers every query, export and downstream copy of the table. Data rules like GDPR usually require deliberate, limited access to national IDs, and this would remove that control.\n2. **It changes the `name` column for everyone.** Values like `'An (079123456789)'` would break name searches, joins, deduplication and anything else that reads `name`. Undoing it would mean rolling back the snapshot or parsing the IDs back out.\n\n**Options:**\n- **Keep the data where it is and join when needed.** The sales team, with the right PII access, can run something like:\n  ```sql\n  SELECT c.id, c.name, p.national_id\n  FROM db.customers c JOIN db.customers_pii p ON p.customer_id = c.id;\n  ```\n- **Show only part of the ID**, such as the last 4 digits (`'An (…6789)'`), if they just need to tell customers apart.\n- **Go ahead as asked** if you confirm that the sales team is authorised to see national IDs and that putting them in `db.customers` is approved. I'd still suggest adding a separate column instead of changing `name`, but I can do it either way.\n\nWhich would you like?", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1523, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1029, "output_tokens": 670, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 75}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
